---
extras: ["nocull"]
title: Placing the exit
---
Put the exit near a point you choose, or let a Dijkstra map find the tile that is farthest from the start [[t:244-250 s:26 s:27]].

## The rule
{% table label="Where the exit goes, by setting" rowheads=true %}
* Setting
* The exit goes on
---
* `right` (c18)
* the open tile nearest the middle of the right edge [[c18:92-109]]
---
* `farthest` (c19)
* the tile with the largest walking distance from the start, read from a Dijkstra map [[c19:92-101]]
{% /table %}

Then the route from the start to the exit is found [[c18:111 c19:103]].

- **Talk says,** of `farthest`: the least accessible part of the map, for when you really dislike your player [[t:249-250]].
- **Talk says,** with a start in the middle: a really bad idea for an exit, and a great way to hide something [[t:249-256]].

## Step through it
@@steps limit=4

## Controls
@@control at
`right`: the open tile nearest the middle of the right edge [[c18:92-109]]. `farthest`: the tile with the largest walking distance from the start [[c19:92-101]].

## What it produces, measured
@@measured

- **Left edge to right:** a route of {{c18.path.median}} steps at the median [[run:c18.path.median]].
- **Center to farthest:** {{c19.path.median}} [[run:c19.path.median]].
  - **Why the least accessible exit is the nearer one:** a start in the middle has less map on any side of it [[own]].

## Where it fails
@@fails

- **Without the cull, it fails:** in a recipe of our own, the same pipeline without its cull, the exit lands in a cave the start can’t reach on {{nocull.fails.exit-unreachable}} of 200 seeds [[run:nocull.fails.exit-unreachable]]. [Seed 0]({{recipe:nocull}}) is one.

